      "id": "v2/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top2/r03/G4",
      "evidence_sha256": "bf433c2f50c4f6f8e96c9d7cfea3b2dc4df62b740636114beea61dd04b8d4900",
      "assessment": "R3 G4 retrieves a correctly oriented comparison to the earlier tick6 schedule and proposes restoration plus a deliberately higher-risk tick8 probe. It appropriately treats the latter as testing response shape, not expected benefit. However r01 and latest differ in two windows; a near-null separate mid edit does not make this exact one-component isolation. Contribution arithmetic again mixes per-pair, whole Mean and fraction of Mean change.",
      "decision_update": "[6,5,6,5] is selected as R4 G1; [8,5,6,5] is not. The restore reproduces an array already present in the same round. Evaluate the information value of another replay against the unselected shape probe without asserting that tick8 would help.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The source branch is not the physical common next parent, and all historical groups do not share one pre-round snapshot. Small gradient/native ratio cannot establish geometry is non-discriminating. Strong Mean despite fewer pair wins remains a legitimate objective observation.",
