    {
      "id": "v2/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top2/r03/synthesis",
      "evidence_sha256": "75cd8f414fed8a6453962f36ce78b2c30b71ce975b04688cdc02ce0448724072",
      "assessment": "R3 council combines all same-wave contrasts, preserves the supported early setting and selects three downward diagnostics plus a repeated schedule reference. This is more varied than Top1’s late repetitions. It still labels [6,5,6,5] the strongest Mean despite [6,6,5,6] being slightly higher, and calls that small lead within noise although it explicitly admits no noise estimate.",
      "decision_update": "R4 executes [6,5,6,5], [6,4,6,5], [6,5,6,4], [6,6,4,6]. It rejects base replay, a second conditional index1-down, untested index1-up7 and index0-up8. This choice covers new downward response with two rounds left, but the repeated reference needs a stated restoration-context or attribution purpose.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "It propagates geometry-cannot-rank and all-other-windows-inert too broadly. The loss/gain from concentrated candidates is not invalidated by flat medians; quality and contribution diagnostics, not an invented breadth threshold, should qualify confidence.",
