    {
      "id": "v2/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top2/r04/G1",
      "evidence_sha256": "fe9f0abbd351f761a83f4755bdc93eb7355724f6de222c2d28d37cc11d2b8a3f",
      "assessment": "R4 G1 retrieves an actual isolated index2 comparison (-0.000022), useful after the previous exchange misattribution. Its main ledger still copies r01 Mean/Best as latest, and it wrongly says only two legal neighbours remain or that returning index2 from6 to5 exhausts all downward levels. It labels any effect below 0.05 inert, an unsupported threshold.",
      "decision_update": "[6,5,6,4] is selected for R5 G2, repeating the current peer; [6,4,6,5] is rejected after synthesis sees the peer’s concentrated loss. The private proposals are understandable given peer privacy, but council should account for current outcomes and justify replay information value.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "Calling small delivery the explanation for flat affinity is stronger than the evidence. A measured nonzero response carried by one candidate would still affect Mean. Global neighbourhood exhaustion cannot be inferred from the small inherited path.",
