    {
      "id": "v2/5nn4_SC2_A_1017__top2/r04/G2",
      "evidence_sha256": "1b823a721f1b4d8784a67701001a53f6f8b36246b91004e5d2967c6d1e08f000",
      "assessment": "R4 G2 directly observes -0.015715 from reducing index1, almost exactly explained by a -1.57773 contributor. It then dismisses this as inert except an artifact, despite the Mean objective and no trace evidence. It incorrectly infers 97/99 pairs within a band from q10/q90; those quantiles do not establish such counts.",
      "decision_update": "Restoration [6,5,6,5] executes as R5 G1 and recovers +0.015715, supporting a repeatable conditional effect rather than erasing it as noise. [5,5,6,5] is unselected. The restoration is sensible, but its written falsifier has the wrong sign and the transfer-versus-loss wording reverses its own forecast.",
      "counterexample_or_limitation": "The claim about almost all pairs is contradicted by additional extrema outside the quoted interval. Quality is acknowledged unknown. A one-candidate loss can be a real schedule response; contribution concentration qualifies generality, not whether the loss counts.",
